&lt;p&gt;Our mission has remained the same even as AI has advanced: to empower developers to ship better software more quickly, freeing them to focus on the creative and rewarding aspects of their work. If you want to help define what development looks like in the agentic era at a company where your work reaches hundreds of thousands of engineers every day, we&#39;d love to have you. For more information on our team and culture, we highly recommend reading our&lt;a href=&quot;https://warpdev.notion.site/Public-Warp-How-We-Work-b872d41a1da743fca18220a731aeba48&quot;&gt;&#39; How We Work&#39; &lt;/a&gt;guide.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Th&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;e Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a rare opportunity to join Warp at a pivotal moment in our growth and become the first engineer focused specifically on Enterprise Security.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Software Engineer, Enterprise Security, you&#39;ll help define and build the security capabilities that allow the world&#39;s most security-conscious organizations to adopt Warp and agentic software development. You&#39;ll work as a product engineer—designing and shipping capabilities across identity, authorization, agent permissions, auditability, data protection, and enterprise controls—while bringing deep security expertise to the decisions we make about the product.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a hands-on software engineering role. You&#39;ll work directly in the Warp codebase, own major technical areas end-to-end, and partner closely with Product and GTM to understand what sophisticated enterprises need from Warp and turn those needs into great product experiences.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and build enterprise security capabilities across areas like identity, authorization, permissions, auditability, policy, data controls, and administration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define the security model for agentic software development, including how agents access code, tools, credentials, customer data, and other sensitive resources.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own major security-sensitive product areas end-to-end, from understanding customer needs and defining the right product behavior through architecture, implementation, launch, and iteration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Product and GTM to understand enterprise security requirements and translate them into product investments that unlock adoption without compromising Warp&#39;s usability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set technical direction for enterprise security at Warp, identifying the highest-leverage capabilities and architectural investments as our product and enterprise business grow.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bring security expertise to the broader engineering organization, helping teams make good architectural decisions around authentication, authorization, isolation, data protection, and other security-sensitive systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Must Have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of professional software engineering experience, ideally building complex production systems in a fast-paced product or startup environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong software engineering fundamentals and a track record of personally designing, building, and shipping significant product or platform capabilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building security-sensitive enterprise features or systems, such as authentication and authorization, RBAC/ABAC, SSO/SCIM, permissions and policy systems, audit logging, tenant isolation, secrets management, encryption, or data controls.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong security intuition and the ability to reason deeply about trust boundaries, permissions, credentials, data access, and how systems can be misused.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong product judgment: you can understand what enterprise customers are trying to accomplish and translate security requirements into pragmatic, usable product experiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to lead ambiguous technical areas as a senior IC: identify the problem, develop an approach, align stakeholders, and drive implementation through completion.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear, thoughtful communication across engineering, Product, GTM, and technically sophisticated customers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable operating with significant ownership and ambiguity—you default to figuring things out rather than waiting to be told what to do.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice to Have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience as a Senior or Staff engineer owning enterprise security, identity, authorization, trust, or governance capabilities at a developer-tool, AI, cloud, security-product, or enterprise SaaS company.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building products used by security teams, CISOs, or enterprise administrators, giving you firsthand understanding of how sophisticated organizations think about security.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working directly with enterprise customers or GTM teams to turn customer security requirements into product capabilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience securing AI or agentic systems, particularly around scoped permissions, untrusted code execution, sandboxing/isolation, secrets and credentials, tool access, approval flows, or access to customer data.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building security products or developer-facing security systems at companies such as Wiz, Snyk, Semgrep, Cloudflare, or similar.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with application security, threat modeling, vulnerability response, or security incidents. These are valuable complementary skills, but this role&#39;s primary focus is building product.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Salary Transparency&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Warp operates from a place of high trust and transparency around compensation. We state the pay range that best aligns with our understanding of the market and the needs for the open role.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;When we find the right person, we try to put our best foot forward with an offer that excites you. We consider your skills, the level of experience you bring, and what similar jobs in the market pay, all while ensuring equal pay for equal work at Warp.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Total compensation at Warp consists of: (1) a market-competitive base salary, (2) a generous benefits package, and (3) meaningful equity.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The budgeted compensation amount for this role is targeted at&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;$230,000 to 290,000&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Exact compensation will vary based on skills and experience.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In addition to salary, all employees receive further compensation in the form of equity in the company. This is a meaningful stock option grant with a four-year vesting period and one-year cliff. Your equity is where most of the significant upside potential is. Comparing startup equity is always a bit tricky, so we’re happy to walk you through different valuation scenarios at the offer stage in order to help paint a clearer picture of the upside.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we offer&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Competitive salary, generous benefits, and meaningful equity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;100% coverage on medical, dental, and vision benefits for employees (80% coverage for dependents)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A flexible remote-first culture, with optional office spaces in NYC and SF for folks who want to work together IRL&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Pre-tax FSA and Health Savings Plans&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Pre-tax Commuter Benefit&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;12 company holidays, 20 days of Paid Time Off, and unlimited sick time&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;16 weeks of paid Parental Leave for both birthing and non-birthing parents&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Twice-a-year all company retreats in awesome locations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A monthly gym and internet stipend&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A company-sponsored 401(k) through Vestwell&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A complimentary OneMedical membership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Individuals seeking employment at Warp are considered without regard to race, color, religion, national origin, age, sex, marital status, ancestry, physical or mental disability, veteran status, gender identity, or sexual orientation.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Warp&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are a company run by product-first builders, building a core product for all developers. We are committed to understanding our users deeply. We will ultimately build the best product and business if that team includes developers and designers from a wide range of backgrounds. The early team comes from Google, Dropbox, Gem, LinkedIn, and Facebook. We are looking for passionate individuals to join us and help bring Warp to the world.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We value honesty, humility, and pragmatism, and our core product principle is focusing on the user. If you’re interested in learning more about our company values and&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;margin: 0px; padding: 0px;&quot;&gt;the culture of our engineering team, please take a look at our internal&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;http://warp.dev/how-we-work&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;&#39;How We Work&#39;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&amp;nbsp;guide.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We’re very fortunate to be backed by a great group of venture capital firms. In August 2023, we announced a $50M Series B funding round ($73M total raised), led by Sequoia Capital.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Our other investors include Google Ventures, Neo, and Box Group. We are also backed by a network of passionate angels, including Dylan Field (Co-Founder and CEO,&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.linkedin.com/pulse/why-im-leading-warps-series-dylan-field/&quot;&gt;Figma&lt;/a&gt;), Elad Gil (early investor in Airbnb, Pinterest, Stripe, and Square), Jeff Weiner (Executive Chairman and Ex-CEO, LinkedIn), Marc Benioff (Founder and CEO, Salesforce), and Sam Altman (Co-Founder &amp;amp; CEO, OpenAI).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
